    "https://unomaha.peopleadmin.com/postings/26037": {
      "title": "University of Nebraska Omaha Portal",
      "description": "University of Nebraska Omaha Portal | Lead Plant Operator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lead Plant Operator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The University of Nebraska at Omaha is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to preventing and eliminating discrimination against employees and prospective employees based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. The University of Nebraska at Omaha does not condone or tolerate discrimination. In support of this policy, the University has implemented employment programs to recruit, employ, and promote qualified individuals based solely on their knowledge, skills, abilities and talents. These factors, along with our commitment to recruit, assess and select all candidates/employees using job-related criteria, ensure fairness, equal evaluation, and treatment in our selection decisions and processes. Requisiton Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu.  Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its education programs or activities, including admissions and employment. The University prohibits any form of retaliation taken against anyone for reporting discrimination, harassment, or retaliation for otherwise engaging in protected activity. Read the full statement. Job Title Lead Plant Operator Job Grade FP18H Division Business and Finance College/Dept Facilities Management and Planning Department Maintenance, Operations and Utilities Requisition Number 2026-00279 FTE (full-time equivalency) 100.00 Work Schedule Sunday - Thursday 7am-3pm Does the position provide the opportunity to work Remotely/Telecommuting? No remote/telecommute opportunity Appointment Term 12- 12/12 months Is this position essential personnel according to the inclement weather policy? Pay Information $60,700-$75,000 Pay Schedule Hourly FLSA Designation Non-Exempt Position Summary Supervise, mentor/coach, assign, coordinate, and inspect work performed by Plant Operators. Operate, monitor, and maintain all equipment in the University’s Central Utility Plant ( CUP ) and other buildings on campus in a safe and efficient manner. Requires knowledge of building systems and maintenance relating to commercial boilers, chillers, HVAC , cooling tower, chemical treatment and refrigeration systems, and all codes and supporting documentation that apply to each. Must be able to interpret schematics, one-line diagrams, and construction drawings. Make rounds and complete operating logs, monitor campus equipment through the energy management system, note deficiencies, and take corrective action. Perform preventive maintenance tasks as well as determine the need for equipment maintenance, diagnosing causes of wear & tear and recommending solutions to problems found. Requires knowledge of commercial HVAC automatic control systems, building electrical systems, and all related components. Conduct routine utility systems inspections and respond to emergency calls in other buildings and grounds on UNO campus during evening, weekend and holiday hours. Job Duties Responsibility Area: Operate & Monitor Equipment Duties: Operate, monitor, and maintain all equipment located within the CUP and other buildings on campus. Components include but not limited to chillers, boilers, cooling towers, air handling units, pumps, air compressors, emergency generators, water softeners, chemical test equipment, etc. Interpret and use schematics, one- line diagrams, and construction drawings to troubleshoot and repair systems and equipment in a commercial setting. Ensure compliance with regulations including all applicable building, boiler, electrical and fire codes, university and departmental standards and guidelines. Percentage Of Time 55 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Preventative Maintenance & Minor Repairs Duties: Supervise, mentor/coach, assign, coordinate, and inspect work performed by Plant Operators. Coordinate equipment and supply purchases for the CUP . Prepare performance evaluations, conduct training, and assign work orders to Plant Operators as required. Ensure that staff have the supplies, tools and equipment required to complete their work successfully. Percentage Of Time 20 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Complete Paperwork Duties: Assign, review, and close-out completed preventive maintenance and service work order requests from staff using the TMA work order system. Approve weekly timecards submitted by your staff. Review and file all inspection reports, log sheets, leave requests, and other required paperwork. Percentage Of Time 10 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: General Housekeeping Duties Duties: Maintain, perform preventative maintenance, and complete repairs on all equipment within the CUP as required. Must be able to use basic hand tools, tube cleaning equipment, lifts, stack gas analyzer, chemical test equipment, volt/ohm/amp meters, and other specialized tools and equipment related to the trade. Percentage Of Time 10 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Supervision & Coordination Duties: Respond to trouble calls received outside of normal university hours and take the appropriate course of action based on conditions of the situation. Percentage Of Time 5 Essential Function: Yes Required and Preferred Qualifications Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Required Experience Five years’ experience with large commercial HVAC equipment and building mechanical systems. Three years’ experience in hands-on boiler and chiller operation. One year of experience with computerized energy management systems. Required License/Certification City of Omaha Third Grade Stationary Engineers License – must be obtained within 6 months of hire date. Valid Driver’s License Required Additional Qualifications: NA Preferred Education Associates degree in Stationary Engineering or equivalent. Preferred Experience Preferred License/Certification Preferred Additional Qualifications: Compliance Requirements Credit Check No Motor Vehicle Licensing Validity Check Yes Pre-employment Physical Request and Assessment Yes Drug Screen Yes Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have at least five years’ experience with large commercial HVAC equipment and building mechanical systems? Yes No * Do you have a valid driver's license? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter University of Nebraska-Lincoln University of Nebraska Medical Center UNO is an EO/Affirmative Action Employer University of Nebraska System Office University of Nebraska at Kearney To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unomaha.peopleadmin.com/postings/26475": {
      "title": "University of Nebraska Omaha Portal | Assistant Director, Packaging",
      "description": "University of Nebraska Omaha Portal | Assistant Director, Packaging Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Director, Packaging Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The University of Nebraska at Omaha is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to preventing and eliminating discrimination against employees and prospective employees based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. The University of Nebraska at Omaha does not condone or tolerate discrimination. In support of this policy, the University has implemented employment programs to recruit, employ, and promote qualified individuals based solely on their knowledge, skills, abilities and talents. These factors, along with our commitment to recruit, assess and select all candidates/employees using job-related criteria, ensure fairness, equal evaluation, and treatment in our selection decisions and processes. Requisiton Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu.  Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its education programs or activities, including admissions and employment. The University prohibits any form of retaliation taken against anyone for reporting discrimination, harassment, or retaliation for otherwise engaging in protected activity. Read the full statement. Job Title Assistant Director, Packaging Job Grade AS23S Division Institutional Effectiveness and Student Success College/Dept Financial Support and Scholarship Department FS&S Requisition Number 2026-00285 FTE (full-time equivalency) 100.00 Work Schedule Monday-Friday, 8AM-5PM, some nights and weekends Does the position provide the opportunity to work Remotely/Telecommuting? No remote/telecommute opportunity Appointment Term 12- 12/12 months Is this position essential personnel according to the inclement weather policy? No Pay Information 52,000 Pay Schedule Annually FLSA Designation Exempt Position Summary Reporting to the Associate Director, Packaging and Loans, the Assistant Director is responsible for overseeing the financial aid packaging process, ensuring compliance with federal and state financial aid regulations, as well as institutional packaging guidelines. This role involves packaging batches of students through an automated process, as well as manual packaging students on an individual basis. The Assistant Director will provide direct supervision to the Financial Support Coordinator, Loans. This position also processes post-packaging reports, over-award reports, third party reports, uncashed warrants, death protocols, less than half time reports, and loan checklists and service indicators. This position will serve as a backup for loan certifying processes. The Assistant Director works with the systems team to set up and test the batch packaging process annually. This position assists with developing and updating all policies and procedures related to packaging and other responsibilities to ensure alignment with federal regulations and institutional goals. Job Duties Responsibility Area: Financial Aid Packaging Administration Duties: Administer and oversee the awarding and packaging of federal financial aid. Perform both mass and manual packaging processes to ensure students receive accurate and timely financial aid offers in accordance with federal regulations, as well as institutional policies and guidelines. Review and resolve complex packaging scenarios and collaborate with staff to support the effective delivery of student aid. Percentage Of Time 30 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Supervising Duties: Directly supervise the Financial Support Coordinator, Loans responsible for federal loan processing. Provide leadership, training, workflow management, and performance oversight to ensure accurate, timely, and compliant administration of Direct Loans, Parent PLUS Loans, Graduate PLUS Loans, and alternative loan programs while supporting exceptional service to students and families. Percentage Of Time 20 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Manual Financial Aid Processing and Special Programs Administration Duties: Perform specialized financial aid processing activities that require individual review and intervention. Responsibilities include administration of the UNO Vets tuition waiver program, processing death protocols, managing uncashed warrants, reviewing third-party reports, monitoring less-than-half-time enrollment, and completing other aid-related adjustments to maintain accurate student aid records. Percentage Of Time 15 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Packaging Reports and Monitoring Duties: Manage and review packaging-related reports to ensure the accuracy and compliance of financial aid awards. Monitor post-packaging reports, over-award reports, and other exception reports; identify discrepancies; make necessary adjustments; and ensure compliance with financial aid regulations. Percentage Of Time 15 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Loan Processing Support Duties: Support federal and private loan administration by assisting with certification, eligibility review, processing, and compliance activities. Work collaboratively with loan staff to ensure accurate and timely processing of Title IV and alternative loan programs while maintaining compliance with federal regulations and institutional policies. Percentage Of Time 10 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Student Account Updates Duties: Maintain and update student financial aid records through the management of service indicators and checklist items related to loan processing. Monitor outstanding requirements, remove completed items, and ensure accurate tracking of student eligibility. Percentage Of Time 5 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Other Duties as Assigned Duties: Other Duties as Assigned Percentage Of Time 5 Essential Function: Yes Required and Preferred Qualifications Required Education Bachelor’s Degree Required Experience Minimum two years of professional work experience and/or two years of financial aid experience. Equivalent combination of education and experience will be considered. Required License/Certification NA Required Additional Qualifications: NA Preferred Education Master’s Degree Preferred Experience 5 or more years working in higher education financial aid administration, specifically with Title IV funds and private loan administration. Preferred License/Certification NASFAA Credential for Packaging & Aid Notification, Direct Loans, Federal Pell Grant Program, etc. Preferred Additional Qualifications: Compliance Requirements Credit Check No Motor Vehicle Licensing Validity Check No Pre-employment Physical Request and Assessment No Drug Screen No Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education you have attained? none High School Diploma/GED Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Master's Degree Doctorate (PhD, MD,EdD, JD etc) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents University of Nebraska-Lincoln University of Nebraska Medical Center UNO is an EO/Affirmative Action Employer University of Nebraska System Office University of Nebraska at Kearney To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
