 genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its education programs or activities, including admissions and employment. The University prohibits any form of retaliation taken against anyone for reporting discrimination, harassment, or retaliation for otherwise engaging in protected activity. Read the full statement. Job Title Facilities Operator | Mon - Fri 8:00AM - 5:00PM Job Grade FP16H Division Business and Finance College/Dept Facilities Management and Planning Department Maintenance, Operations and Utilities Requisition Number 2026-00259 FTE (full-time equivalency) 100 Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8am - 5pm Does the position provide the opportunity to work Remotely/Telecommuting? No remote/telecommute opportunity Appointment Term 12- 12/12 months Is this position essential personnel according to the inclement weather policy? Pay Information $24.00-$30.00/hour depending on experience Pay Schedule Hourly FLSA Designation Non-Exempt Position Summary Operate, maintain, install, and perform preventive maintenance on all types of heating, air conditioning, and refrigeration equipment including large commercial air handlers, boilers, chillers, pumps, generators, AC split systems, air compressors, and other related equipment. Requires general knowledge of building systems and maintenance relating to commercial HVAC systems. Requires general knowledge of commercial HVAC automatic control systems, building electrical systems, commercial plumbing systems, and all related components. Requires some experience with commercial plumbing systems, fixtures, and related components. Perform carpentry work throughout campus, such as repairs to doors and door hardware, ceilings, flooring, and classroom seating. This position will be expected to interact with customers and other employees in a professional manner that enhances work effectiveness for the facilities maintenance crew. Assist Plant Operators as directed. Perform all duties of that position to include, but not limited to, operating central utilities plant equipment, make rounds and complete operating logs, monitor campus equipment through the energy management systems, note deficiencies and take corrective action. Job Duties Responsibility Area: Maintenance Duties: Operate, maintain, install, and perform preventive maintenance on all types of heating, air conditioning, and refrigeration equipment including large commercial air handlers, boilers, chillers, pumps, generators, AC split systems, air compressors, and other related equipment. Ensure compliance with regulations including all applicable building, electrical and fire codes, university and departmental standards and guidelines. Assist with major rebuilds and repairs on equipment as required. Percentage Of Time 60 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Carpentry Work Duties: Perform carpentry work throughout campus, such as repairs to doors and door hardware, ceilings, flooring, furniture, and classroom seating. Percentage Of Time 15 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Emergency Repairs Duties: Respond to calls from supervisor, control systems operator, or facilities service dispatcher that require immediate action. Diagnosis problem and take appropriate action. Percentage Of Time 10 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Work Orders Duties: Document completed preventive maintenance and work order requests using the Computer Maintenance Management System ( CMMS ). Complete material request forms, inspection reports, log sheets, leave requests, and other required paperwork. Percentage Of Time 5 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Central Utility Plant work Duties: Assist Plant Operators as needed. Perform all duties of that position to include, but not limited to, operating central utilities plant equipment, make rounds and complete operating logs, monitor campus equipment through the energy management systems, note deficiencies and take corrective action. Percentage Of Time 5 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: General Housekeeping Duties: Perform general housekeeping duties in campus mechanical rooms, utilities manholes and vaults, air shafts, utility tunnels, etc. These include but are not limited to sweeping, washing, painting, etc. Percentage Of Time 5 Essential Function: No Required and Preferred Qualifications Required Education High School Diploma or equivalent . Required Experience One year of experience with HVAC equipment and building mechanical systems, or equivalent education. Required License/Certification Valid Driver’s License Required Additional Qualifications: City of Omaha – Third Grade Engineers License (Or the ability to obtain within 18 months of hire date) Preferred Education Associates degree in HVAC technology. Preferred Experience One year of experience in hands-on boiler operation. One year of experience with computerized energy management systems. Preferred License/Certification NA Preferred Additional Qualifications: NA Compliance Requirements Credit Check No Motor Vehicle Licensing Validity Check Yes Pre-employment Physical Request and Assessment Yes Drug Screen Yes Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have at least one year of experience with HVAC equipment and building mechanical systems, or equivalent education? Yes No * Do you have a valid driver's license? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter University of Nebraska-Lincoln University of Nebraska Medical Center UNO is an EO/Affirmative Action Employer University of Nebraska System Office University of Nebraska at Kearney To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
