      "description": "University of Nebraska Omaha Portal | Research Assistant - Biomechanics - Other Hourly Worker Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Research Assistant - Biomechanics - Other Hourly Worker Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The University of Nebraska at Omaha is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to preventing and eliminating discrimination against employees and prospective employees based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. The University of Nebraska at Omaha does not condone or tolerate discrimination. In support of this policy, the University has implemented employment programs to recruit, employ, and promote qualified individuals based solely on their knowledge, skills, abilities and talents. These factors, along with our commitment to recruit, assess and select all candidates/employees using job-related criteria, ensure fairness, equal evaluation, and treatment in our selection decisions and processes. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Research Assistant - Biomechanics - Other Hourly Worker Department Biomechanics Essential Functions Research Support: Conduct experiments, fabricate prototypes, and assist faculty and students with NE3D research projects. Equipment Management: Operate, maintain, calibrate, troubleshoot, and document use of 3D printers and other laboratory equipment. Data Collection: Collect, organize, analyze, and maintain research data and laboratory records. Education & Outreach: Support student training, workshops, K–12 programs, demonstrations, summer programs, and community engagement. Center Documentation: Track and document research activities, equipment utilization, participants, milestones, outcomes, publications, and other information needed for NSF reporting and evaluation. Work Schedule Additional Duties Required Qualifications Research Experience: Experience conducting laboratory research, following experimental protocols, and collecting and organizing scientific data. Additive Manufacturing Skills: Experience with 3D printing, CAD , prototyping, biomechanics, engineering, materials science, or related technologies. Equipment & Technical Skills: Experience operating, maintaining, troubleshooting, and documenting laboratory or research equipment. Communication & Outreach: Experience working with students, researchers, educators, or community partners and supporting training, workshops, or STEM outreach activities. Organization & Documentation: Strong organizational and computer skills with demonstrated ability to maintain research records, equipment logs, project documentation, and reports while managing multiple activities and deadlines. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Regularly sits; may stand, walk. See, hear, speak and use of hands. Work Environment The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Regularly works indoors. Noise level is low to moderate. Salary 18.00/hour Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2026T-00155 Open Date 06/23/2026 Close Date 07/30/2030 Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants The University of Nebraska at Omaha is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to preventing and eliminating discrimination against employees and prospective employees based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. The University of Nebraska at Omaha does not condone or tolerate discrimination. In support of this policy, the University has implemented employment programs to recruit, employ, and promote qualified individuals based solely on their knowledge, skills, abilities and talents. These factors, along with our commitment to recruit, assess and select all candidates/employees using job-related criteria, ensure fairness, equal evaluation, and treatment in our selection decisions and processes. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a degree in Biomechanics, Biomedical Engineering, or another related field? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents University of Nebraska-Lincoln University of Nebraska Medical Center UNO is an EO/Affirmative Action Employer University of Nebraska System Office University of Nebraska at Kearney To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
