    "https://unomaha.peopleadmin.com/postings/26471": {
      "title": "University of Nebraska Omaha Portal | Instructor of Music Technology and Music Industry",
      "description": "University of Nebraska Omaha Portal | Instructor of Music Technology and Music Industry Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Instructor of Music Technology and Music Industry Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Submit applications electronically at the University website: https://unomaha.peopleadmin.com/postings/26234 by October 15, 2026. Please attach 1) a cover letter expressing your interest in the position and 2) a curriculum vitae. Questions about the position may be sent to Dr. Tomm Roland, search chair, at troland@unomaha.edu Posting Details Position Information Job Title Instructor of Music Technology and Music Industry Department School of Music Essential Functions The School of Music seeks a dynamic and collaborative educator to teach in its established, comprehensive music technology program and its recently developed music industry program. Candidates should be accomplished musicians with a wide range of technical skills and expertise in music industry and music technology.  The anticipated start date is August 2027. Teach courses in music technology and music industry. Work collaboratively with all faculty. Willingness to contribute to all aspects of life in the School of Music including active involvement in the recruitment and retention of students and curriculum development. Additional duties related to candidate’s expertise and experience may also be assigned by the Director. Preferred qualifications include substantial experience in both music technology and music industry. Primary teaching responsibilities might include courses in music technology (such as audio recording techniques), music business, music industry studies, multimedia (game audio/film), and commercial music ensemble. The successful candidate will demonstrate versatility in preparing students for today’s varied and evolving professional landscape. Areas of knowledge should include rights and copyright, music business, music production, live music management, stage production, arts management, music administration, and commercial music. Additional potential teaching areas include applied instruction on rock and popular music instruments or in laptop-based performance. The University of Nebraska at Omaha is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to preventing and eliminating discrimination against employees and prospective employees based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. The University of Nebraska at Omaha does not condone or tolerate discrimination. In support of this policy, the University has implemented employment programs to recruit, employ, and promote qualified individuals based solely on their knowledge, skills, abilities and talents. These factors, along with our commitment to recruit, assess and select all candidates/employees using job-related criteria, ensure fairness, equal evaluation, and treatment in our selection decisions and processes. Work Schedule Additional Duties Required Qualifications Master’s degree in Music, eligible for appointment to graduate faculty Preferred Qualifications 1) teaching experience at the university level; 2) experience with recording techniques, music industry, music business Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Regularly sits; may stand, walk. See, hear, speak and use of hands. Work Environment The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Regularly works indoors. Noise level is low to moderate. Salary $51,000 Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2026F-00144 Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Submit applications electronically at the University website: https://unomaha.peopleadmin.com/postings/26234 by October 15, 2026. Please attach 1) a cover letter expressing your interest in the position and 2) a curriculum vitae. Questions about the position may be sent to Dr. Tomm Roland, search chair, at troland@unomaha.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents University of Nebraska-Lincoln University of Nebraska Medical Center UNO is an EO/Affirmative Action Employer University of Nebraska System Office University of Nebraska at Kearney To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
