tal status, and/or political affiliation in its education programs or activities, including admissions and employment. The University prohibits any form of retaliation taken against anyone for reporting discrimination, harassment, or retaliation for otherwise engaging in protected activity. Read the full statement. Job Title Project and Design Manager Job Grade AB21S Division Academic Affairs College/Dept College of Arts and Sciences Department Philosophy Requisition Number 2026-00289 FTE (full-time equivalency) 100.00 Work Schedule Monday through Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Some hours will be necessary after 5:00 p.m. or on weekends with events. Does the position provide the opportunity to work Remotely/Telecommuting? No remote/telecommute opportunity Appointment Term 12- 12/12 months Is this position essential personnel according to the inclement weather policy? Pay Information $52,000 Pay Schedule Annually FLSA Designation Exempt Position Summary Under the supervision of the Executive Director of the Goldstein Center for Human Rights and Director of the Fried Academy, the Project and Design Manager will implement projects, exhibitions, symposiums and other tasks as assigned for the Goldstein Center for Human Rights, Fried Academy, and Goldstein Family Community Chair in Human Rights. This position will be responsible for project design and management. The position will manage communication in multiple media, including email, phone, video, website and social media management. This position will also conduct fundraising and grant writing as well as managing budget documents, record-keeping, and interacting with University financial and record-keeping systems. The Project and Design Manager will supervise student workers. Job Duties Responsibility Area: Supervise student workers Duties: Supervise student workers Percentage Of Time 5 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Project Design Duties: · Project design and management, e.g. events planning and management; developing and implementing a plan for UNO’s hosting of a national consortium of human rights and Holocaust and genocide studies centers 40% Percentage Of Time 40 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Internal and external business communications Duties: Internal and external business communications, e.g. facilitating interactions among Center faculty and other partners; professional interaction with the public and with faculty and administrators from multiple universities; marketing and public relations; and social media 25% Percentage Of Time 25 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Adminsitrative Duties Duties: Budget management, record-keeping, and other administrative tasks Percentage Of Time 20 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Fundraising and Development Duties: Fundraising and Development Percentage Of Time 10 Essential Function: Yes Required and Preferred Qualifications Required Education Master’s Degree Required Experience Three or more years of professional administrative experience Required License/Certification Required Additional Qualifications: Preferred Education Master’s Degree in human rights, Holocaust and genocide studies, or a cognate field Preferred Experience Three or more years of professional administrative experience in higher education Preferred License/Certification Preferred Additional Qualifications: Compliance Requirements Credit Check No Motor Vehicle Licensing Validity Check No Pre-employment Physical Request and Assessment No Drug Screen No Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education you have attained? none High School Diploma/GED Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Master's Degree Doctorate (PhD, MD,EdD, JD etc) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter University of Nebraska-Lincoln University of Nebraska Medical Center UNO is an EO/Affirmative Action Employer University of Nebraska System Office University of Nebraska at Kearney To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
