tity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its education programs or activities, including admissions and employment. The University prohibits any form of retaliation taken against anyone for reporting discrimination, harassment, or retaliation for otherwise engaging in protected activity. Read the full statement. Job Title Administrative Coordinator- CAS Deans Office and Schwalb Center Job Grade AB14H Division Academic Affairs College/Dept College of Arts and Sciences Department CAS Requisition Number 2026-00300 FTE (full-time equivalency) 100.00 Work Schedule Monday through Friday 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. some hours after 5:00 with events Does the position provide the opportunity to work Remotely/Telecommuting? No remote/telecommute opportunity Appointment Term 12- 12/12 months Is this position essential personnel according to the inclement weather policy? No Pay Information $22.11 per hour - $23.076 per hour Pay Schedule Hourly FLSA Designation Non-Exempt Position Summary As an employee of the Dean’s Office in the College of Arts and Sciences, this position provides comprehensive administrative, financial, and HR/payroll support for the Schwalb Center and the Dean’s Office. This position supports daily operations, coordinates events and meetings, manages budget-related activities for the Schwalb Center, and assists the CAS Business Manager with personnel and payroll processes. The role requires strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to handle confidential information. This position also requires use of independent judgment and knowledge college and university policies. Job Duties Responsibility Area: Schwalb Center Administrative Support & Events Coordination Duties: Serve as primary point of contact for phone, email, and in-person inquires Manage incoming and outgoing correspondence, including mail distribution Maintain confidential records through retrieving, retaining, storing, compiling, coding, updating, distributing, and destroying files as appropriate (electronic and paper) Coordinate office operations, including supplies, equipment maintenance, and work orders Maintain Center calendars and schedules Assist with research activities for the Center Coordinate meetings, programs, and events (space reservations, logistics, catering, speakers, and materials) Prepare and distribute event communications and promotional materials, in conjunction with the Marketing and Communications Manager Maintain databases, contact lists, and administrative systems Support website updates and social media content as needed Percentage Of Time 30 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Schwalb Center Budget/Financial Administration Duties: Monitor, reconcile, and track Center budgets and expenditures Prepare financial documentation and reports for review and approval Process expenses reimbursements, deposits, and financial transactions Coordinate travel arrangements and related documentation Manage honoraria payments and supporting documentation Track memberships, subscriptions, and related payments Assist and monitor grants as needed Percentage Of Time 20 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Dean's Office HR/Payroll and Business Office Support Duties: Assist the Business manager with HR and payroll processes Prepare and process Personnel Actional Forms (PAFs) for new hires, rehires, funding changes, and separations/ end appointments and Recurring Payment forms (FPs) Assist with part-time instruction payment processing Assist with reappointment letters and employment -related correspondence Review and verify bi-weekly and monthly payroll for accuracy Track employee appointments, contract terms, and renewal deadlines Maintain confidential personnel records in compliance with university policies Assist with the coordination of onboarding and offboarding processes Percentage Of Time 35 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Other Duties Duties: Perform all other duties as assigned Percentage Of Time 15 Essential Function: No Required and Preferred Qualifications Required Education High school education or equivalent Required Experience Two years of progressively responsible administrative support experience Experience with financial recordkeeping and basic budget tracking Required License/Certification n/a Required Additional Qualifications: n/a Preferred Education Bachelor’s degree in business administration, public administration or related field Preferred Experience Experience in higher education or a similar institutional environment Experience with SAP , PeopleAdmin, or similar HR/payroll systems Experience coordinating events or programs Preferred License/Certification n/a Preferred Additional Qualifications: n/a Compliance Requirements Credit Check No Motor Vehicle Licensing Validity Check No Pre-employment Physical Request and Assessment No Drug Screen No Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe your administrative and budget experience. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents University of Nebraska-Lincoln University of Nebraska Medical Center UNO is an EO/Affirmative Action Employer University of Nebraska System Office University of Nebraska at Kearney To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unomaha.peopleadmin.com/postings/26214": {
      "title": "University of Nebraska Omaha Portal",
      "description": "University of Nebraska Omaha Portal | Facilities Operator | Tues - Sat 7:00AM - 4:00PM Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Facilities Operator | Tues - Sat 7:00AM - 4:00PM Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Requisiton Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu.  Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. GENERAL REQUISITION INFORMATION EEO Statement: The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its education programs or activities, including admissions and employment. The University prohibits any form of retaliation taken against anyone for reporting discrimination, harassment, or retaliation for otherwise engaging in protected activity. Read the full statement. Job Title Facilities Operator | Tues - Sat 7:00AM - 4:00PM Job Grade FP16H Division Business and Finance College/Dept Facilities Management and Planning Department Maintenance, Operations and Utilities Requisition Number 2026-00293 FTE (full-time equivalency) 100 Work Schedule Tuesday - Saturday 7am - 4pm Does the position provide the opportunity to work Remotely/Telecommuting? No remote/telecommute opportunity Appointment Term 12- 12/12 months Is this position essential personnel according to the inclement weather policy? Pay Information $25.39 - $30.00/hr Pay Schedule Hourly FLSA Designation Non-Exempt Position Summary Operate, maintain, install, and perform preventive maintenance on all types of heating, air conditioning, and refrigeration equipment including large commercial air handlers, boilers, chillers, pumps, generators, AC split systems, air compressors, and other related equipment. Requires general knowledge of building systems and maintenance relating to commercial HVAC systems. Requires general knowledge of commercial HVAC automatic control systems, building electrical systems, commercial plumbing systems, and all related components. Requires some experience with commercial plumbing systems, fixtures, and related components. Perform carpentry work throughout campus, such as repairs to doors and door hardware, ceilings, flooring, and classroom seating. This position will be expected to interact with customers and other employees in a professional manner that enhances work effectiveness for the facilities maintenance crew. Assist Plant Operators as directed. Perform all duties of that position to include, but not limited to, operating central utilities plant equipment, make rounds and complete operating logs, monitor campus equipment through the energy management systems, note deficiencies and take corrective action. Job Duties Responsibility Area: Maintenance Duties: Operate, maintain, install, and perform preventive maintenance on all types of heating, air conditioning, and refrigeration equipment including large commercial air handlers, boilers, chillers, pumps, generators, AC split systems, air compressors, and other related equipment. Ensure compliance with regulations including all applicable building, electrical and fire codes, university and departmental standards and guidelines. Assist with major rebuilds and repairs on equipment as required. Percentage Of Time 60 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Carpentry Work Duties: Perform carpentry work throughout campus, such as repairs to doors and door hardware, ceilings, flooring, furniture, and classroom seating. Percentage Of Time 15 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Emergency Repairs Duties: Respond to calls from supervisor, control systems operator, or facilities service dispatcher that require immediate action. Diagnosis problem and take appropriate action. Percentage Of Time 10 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Work Orders Duties: Document completed preventive maintenance and work order requests using the Computer Maintenance Management System ( CMMS ). Complete material request forms, inspection reports, log sheets, leave requests, and other required paperwork. Percentage Of Time 5 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: Central Utility Plant work Duties: Assist Plant Operators as needed. Perform all duties of that position to include, but not limited to, operating central utilities plant equipment, make rounds and complete operating logs, monitor campus equipment through the energy management systems, note deficiencies and take corrective action. Percentage Of Time 5 Essential Function: Yes Responsibility Area: General Housekeeping Duties: Perform general housekeeping duties in campus mechanical rooms, utilities manholes and vaults, air shafts, utility tunnels, etc. These include but are not limited to sweeping, washing, painting, etc. Percentage Of Time 5 Essential Function: No Required and Preferred Qualifications Required Education High School Diploma or equivalent . Required Experience One years’ experience with HVAC equipment and building mechanical systems, or equivalent education. Required License/Certification Valid Driver’s License Required Additional Qualifications: City of Omaha – Third Grade Engineers License (Or the ability to obtain within 18 months of hire date) Preferred Education Associates degree in HVAC technology. Preferred Experience One year of experience in hands-on boiler operation. One year of experience with computerized energy management systems. Preferred License/Certification Preferred Additional Qualifications: Compliance Requirements Credit Check No Motor Vehicle Licensing Validity Check Yes Pre-employment Physical Request and Assessment Yes Drug Screen Yes Supplemental Question Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter University of Nebraska-Lincoln University of Nebraska Medical Center UNO is an EO/Affirmative Action Employer University of Nebraska System Office University of Nebraska at Kearney To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
